From: plastron
Subject: [PATCH] PX30 (GKD Pixel 2): the chip's own reset restarts the RK817 too

A watchdog's reset (zytest=hang on 1.1.1-test.2, 2026-11-26) never started
ZyperOS again: the reset was the PX30's alone, the RK817 stayed on, so
vccio_sd stayed at 1.8 V and the card in its SDR104 signalling, which the
boot ROM cannot read at 3.3 V, and it started the handheld's own loader
instead (its charging screen, then its red "system failure").

Now, in the board's late init, at every start (the RK817's restart sets its
registers back): GPIO0_A4 in its function 2, the SoC's reset out, and the
RK817's sleep pin set to reset the whole PMU, active low, as Rockchip's own
kernel does (rk808's "pmic-reset" state). Only when the line reads high
there. Measured on that Pixel 2 with the registers set by hand: the
watchdog's reset came back in ZyperOS 16 s later, no button, the RAM and
pstore kept, ON_SOURCE 0x04. A start with that reason is never a
charger's, and sets zy_reset=chip, which boot.scr puts on the kernel's line
as zyreset=chip for ZyperOS's crashlog.
---
--- a/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
+++ b/board/hardkernel/odroid_go2/go2.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <power/pmic.h>
 #include <power/rk8xx_pmic.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 
 #define DTB_DIR			"rockchip/"
 
@@ -114,6 +115,55 @@
  * own there (0x02, read on a Pixel 2 on 2026-11-06, against 0x40 for the
  * charger), so one never comes back as a charger's start.
  */
+/*
+ * plastron: the PX30's own resets (its watchdog, its thermal cut-off) are a
+ * restart of the RK817 too, as Rockchip's own kernel sets it up (rk808's
+ * "pmic-reset" state: GPIO0_A4 in its function 2, the SoC's reset out, and
+ * the RK817's sleep pin set to reset, active low). Alone, the chip's reset
+ * left the RK817 on: vccio_sd at 1.8 V and the card in its SDR104
+ * signalling, which the boot ROM cannot read at 3.3 V, so it started the
+ * handheld's own loader instead (its charging screen, then its red "system
+ * failure": a Pixel 2 on 1.1.1-test.2, 2026-11-26). With the RK817's
+ * restart (RST_FUNC 0, the whole PMU, as Linux's DEV_RST) the card is power
+ * cycled and boots, and the RAM, pstore's report in it, is kept: measured on
+ * that Pixel 2 the same evening, back in ZyperOS 16 s after the watchdog,
+ * ON_SOURCE 0x04 (Linux's restart is 0x02).
+ *
+ * The RK817's restart sets its registers back, so this is done at every
+ * start. Armed only when the line reads high (idle) in function 2, as it did
+ * on that Pixel 2: low would restart the RK817 at once.
+ */
+#define PX30_PMUGRF_GPIO0A_IOMUX	0xff010000
+#define PX30_GPIO0_EXT_PORTA		0xff040050
+#define PX2_SYS_CFG3_RST_LOW		0x18	/* RST_FUNC 0, SLPPOL low, SLPPIN reset */
+#define PX2_SYS_CFG3_SLP_MASK		0xf8	/* RST_FUNC, SLPPOL, SLPPIN */
+
+static void px2_reset_route(struct udevice *pmic)
+{
+	int i;
+
+	/* GPIO0_A4, bits 9:8, with their write mask */
+	writel(0x3 << (8 + 16) | 0x2 << 8, PX30_PMUGRF_GPIO0A_IOMUX);
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+		udelay(20);
+		if (!(readl(PX30_GPIO0_EXT_PORTA) & BIT(4))) {
+			writel(0x3 << (8 + 16), PX30_PMUGRF_GPIO0A_IOMUX);
+			printf("PMIC reset line low in function 2: not armed\n");
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+	pmic_clrsetbits(pmic, RK817_REG_SYS_CFG3, PX2_SYS_CFG3_SLP_MASK, PX2_SYS_CFG3_RST_LOW);
+}
+
+/*
+ * plastron: a start after the chip's own reset, which the route above made a
+ * restart of the RK817 with a reason of its own in ON_SOURCE (0x04): never a
+ * charger's start, and the kernel's line says so (zy_reset=chip, boot.scr's
+ * zyreset=), so ZyperOS's crashlog reports it as the watchdog's (or the
+ * thermal cut-off's) even with nothing else kept.
+ */
+#define PX2_ON_CHIP_RESET		BIT(2)
+
 static void px2_charge_boot(void)
 {
 	struct udevice *pmic;
@@ -122,6 +172,12 @@
 	if (uclass_get_device_by_driver(UCLASS_PMIC, DM_DRIVER_GET(rockchip_rk805), &pmic))
 		return;
 	on = pmic_reg_read(pmic, RK817_ON_SOURCE);
+	px2_reset_route(pmic);
+	if (on >= 0 && (on & PX2_ON_CHIP_RESET) && !(on & (RK8XX_ON_PWRON | RK8XX_ON_PLUG_IN))) {
+		printf("Started by the chip's own reset (ON_SOURCE 0x%02x): zy_reset=chip\n", on);
+		env_set("zy_reset", "chip");
+		return;
+	}
 	if (on < 0 || !(on & RK8XX_ON_PLUG_IN) || (on & RK8XX_ON_PWRON))
 		return;
 	printf("Started by a charger: zy_charge=1\n");
